Hi,

Why a new system?  Why not just start putting together some stackable   
terminal servers?  Most new ones support TCP/IP and IPX dialup no problem   
 (e.g., Digital's NetRider, Livingston's POP box).  It would be more   
expandable, more generic, and less costly.  Put ManageWORKS on your Alpha   
and you can control and monitor them with SNMP, too.

If you want full RAS integration, with NT-based authentication, and don't   
mind  the dedicated box approach, a small Intel system with a Digiboard   
or some other serial adapter should be adequate, too.

Just some ideas,
Aaron

