Subject: RE: HP Scanjet IIcx ????

The currently available HP Scanner driver on Alpha Windows NT (3.51 &
Beta 4.0) supports 16-bit applications only.

Currently, DeskScan II V2.3 does not work on any Alpha Windows NT
version because it is a 32-bit Intel application. This has not been
tested with FX!32.

However, the older version of DeskScan II V2.0 does work on Alpha
Windows NT 3.51 & Beta 4.0.  Contact the IHV Program Office for a copy
of DeskScan II V2.0 diskette.

Installation Instructions for 3.51:  Perform the following steps to
allow the HP ScanJet II to function properly on 3.51:

1.	Obtain a copy of the DeskScan II V2.0 software diskette from the IHV
Program Office
2.	Copy the DeskScan II V2.0 software to a local disk
3.	Copy the file hpscan32.dll to the directory %SystemRoot%\system32
4.	Add the line device=%SystemRoot%\system32\drivers\hpscan16.sys to the
file %SystemRoot%\system32\config.nt
5.	Reboot the system

