Subject: RE: NT 3.51 Mac File Server Performance Mystery

Robert,

If the power outage damaged, but did not destroy, the SCSI drive on
which your Apple shares are hosted, you could see the sort of behavior
you describe.  I'm hypothesizing that occasional SCSI retries are
causing the slowdown, but not producing hard failures.  You could test
this theory by seeing what performance looks like if you move the server
files to a different drive, and perhaps to a different SCSI adapter,
though you don't say if you have another SCSI adapter, in addition to
the built-in NCR 53C810.

I'd be very surprised if it were related to Service Pack 4, but the fact
that you asked suggests you may have applied SP4 after the power outage.
 Is that the case?

