Date: Tue, 30 Apr 1996 21:03:59 -0700 (PDT)
From: Danny Thorpe <dthorpe@subliminal.com>
Subject: Re: Corrupt Registry File

Reinstalling your existing NT software is almost exactly the same procedure
as installing NT 4.0 over your existing NT installation.  You just install
over what's already there.

It's unlikely that NT 4.0 will do any better job of sorting out a corrupted
registry than the current NT 3.51.

If you created an emergency repair diskette after setting up your NT
machine, then you can use that to try to recover or repair the damaged
registry hives.  Creating/updating the repair disk after major software
installations is a good idea (use RDISK).  You can also restore registry
files from backup tapes to roll the system back to a previous installation.

-Danny

